.TH MC1-SLURM-BUILD-RPMS 1 "2026-10-07" "mu2edaq-batch-queues" "Mu2e DAQ Tools"
.SH NAME
mc1-slurm-build-rpms \- build Slurm RPMs for EL9 and EL10 and fetch them for the deployer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mc1-slurm-build-rpms
.RB [ \-V
.IR version ]
.RB [ \-H
.IR host ]
.RB [ \-j
.IR user@jump ]
.RB [ \-u
.IR user ]
.RB [ \-\-fetch\-only ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The MC1 workers mix AlmaLinux 9 and 10. Their EPEL repositories ship
different Slurm releases (22.05 and 26.05), and slurmd must never be newer than
slurmctld. This tool builds one SchedMD release for both platforms.
.PP
On the build host it downloads
.IR slurm-<version>.tar.bz2
from download.schedmd.com into
.IR /scratch/mc1-slurm-build/src
and records its SHA-256. It then runs
.B rpmbuild \-ta \-\-with mysql
inside
.B quay.io/almalinux/almalinux:9
and
.B :10
podman containers, so build dependencies never touch the host. Finally it
fetches the RPMs into
.IR artifacts/rpms/<version>/el9
and
.IR el10 ,
which are git-ignored. The deployer installs from there
.RB ( slurm_rpm_dir ,
.BR slurm_version )
and version-locks the packages.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Slurm release (env
.BR MC1_SLURM_VERSION ,
default 26.05.4).
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-host
Build host with podman (env
.BR MC1_BUILD_HOST ,
default mu2e-mc1-worker-17.fnal.gov).
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jump
ProxyJump hop (env
.BR MC1_JUMP ).
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user
Login on the build host (env
.BR MC1_SSH_USER ,
default root).
.TP
.B \-\-fetch\-only
Fetch RPMs built earlier; do not rebuild.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
scripts/mc1-slurm-build-rpms
scripts/mc1-slurm-build-rpms \-V 26.05.5
scripts/mc1-slurm-deploy deploy \-\-set slurm_version=26.05.5
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mc1-slurm-deploy (1),
.BR rpmbuild (8),
.BR podman (1)
